= Willie Whitelaw

Deputy Leader and Shadow Home Secretary. He ran against you in 1975 and has been loyal ever since. The wets trust him, which makes him invaluable.

- @soothe_wets
- @discipline
- @law_and_order
- @root: Return

@soothe_wets
title: Calm the wets
subtitle: Greatly reduces wet dissent and softens Heath.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Shadow Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; wet_dissent -= 10; heath_hostility -= 5

Over long dinners at the Carlton Club, Willie persuades the doubters that you will listen to them.

@discipline
title: Party discipline
subtitle: Reduces dissent across the party.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next Shadow Cabinet action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; dry_dissent -= 6; wet_dissent -= 6; loyalist_dissent -= 6; right_dissent -= 6

Willie works the tea room and the smoking room. Nobody wants to be the one who lets him down.

@law_and_order
title: Make law and order our issue
subtitle: Working-class voters and the right respond.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); right_dissent -= 4; wet_dissent += 1

[? if con_in_government = 0 : Whitelaw promises more police, better paid, and tougher sentences. Labour, which has frozen police pay, has no answer. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 : The Home Secretary visits police stations up and down the country. He is booed at the Police Federation conference and cheered at the party conference, which he considers about right. ?]
